sorry_after": 0, "sorry_delta": 0, "decl_after": {}, "decl_delta": {}}, "sorry_delta": 0, "other_count": 28}, {"sha": "c3b44ca39b9d68b6e04ca083445cf0215d1608df", "short_sha": "c3b44ca39b", "subject": "review caught me presenting an ABSENCE OF DERIVATION as a proof of safety", "summary": "**The defect, found by a fresh-context review of the file.** Three sites said the `\u22a4` binders of GlobalGeneration/LedgerClosure/SectionBounds \"survive\" / \"are fine\" at a proper curve, in the same confident register as the two machine-checked claims beside them. What is actually established is only that THIS derivation does not apply there \u2014 an absence of route, not satisfiability. Nothing proves those binders hold at a proper curve: that is finiteness of $L(D)$, Riemann--Roch`s own content, open in AJC.\n\nThis is trap (i) turned on my own correction: I retracted an overstated refutation and replaced it with an overstated safety claim. Corrected at all three sites plus the frontier bullet, with what is proved and what is not now listed separately.\n\nReview also CONFIRMED the mathematics: the fraction-field closing move, the no-affineness-needed order bound, the DVR-is-not-a-field argument, and that no curve-dimension hypothesis leaks into any statement (the file is proved more generally than curves).", "created_at": "2026-07-28T16:56:01+08:00", "role": "horizon", "kind": "agent", "files": [{"path": "MainProjects/Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge/AlgebraicJacobian/RiemannRoch/Adelic/ChartFinitenessRefuted.lean", "category": "lean", "add": 23, "del": 13, "loc_before": 417, "loc_after": 427, "loc_code_before": 176, "loc_code_after": 176, "sorry_before": 0, "sorry_after": 0, "sorry_delta": 0, "decl_before": {"theorem": 12, "def": 2}, "decl_after": {"theorem": 12, "def": 2}, "decl_delta": {}, "added": false, "deleted": false}, {"path": "MainProjects/Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge/scripts/axiom-frontier.lean", "category": "lean", "add": 5, "del": 1, "loc_before": 1355, "loc_after": 1359, "loc_code_before": 261, "loc_code_after": 261, "sorry_before": 0, "sorry_after": 0, "sorry_delta": 0, "decl_before": {"def": 4, "theorem": 14}, "decl_after": {"def": 4, "theorem": 14}, "decl_delta": {}, "added": false, "deleted": false}], "lean": {"files": 2, "add": 28, "del": 14, "loc_after": 1786, "loc_code_after": 437, "loc_delta": 14, "loc_code_delta": 0, "sorry_after": 0, "sorry_delta": 0, "decl_after": {"theorem": 26, "def": 6}, "decl_delta": {}}, "blueprint": {"files": 0, "add": 0, "del": 0, "loc_after": 0, "loc_code_after": 0, "loc_delta": 0, "loc_code_delta": 0, "sorry_after": 0, "sorry_delta": 0, "decl_after": {}, "decl_delta": {}}, "sorry_delta": 0, "other_count": 0}, {"sha": "a905ca4f99016c3a17ab60208124e31a82b5378e", "short_sha": "a905ca4f99", "subject": "NON-VACUITY measured at a synthesis site: the collapse fires at an actual AJC curve bundle", "summary": "**The trap-(d) check, and it took three attempts \u2014 which is the finding.** `ChartFinitenessRefuted` carries `[IsConstantField k X]` and `[Algebra k X.functionField]`, both produced only by SCOPED instances in `Adelic/GateInstances.lean`, so it is exactly the shape \u00a76e catches. (1) With an arbitrary `Algebra k K(C)` supplied by hand, `IsConstantField` does NOT synthesise \u2014 the producer needs the scoped `functionFieldAlgebra` specifically. (2) With the scope opened but `GateInstances` not imported, the algebra itself fails. (3) With both, `not_chart_finite_of_primeDivisor k hU P` elaborates at an AJC curve with only `[IsIntegral] [IsLocallyNoetherian] [IsRegularInCodimensionOne]`.\n\nSo the collapse is not vacuous: it fires at the object the lane runs on. And a consumer that forgets the import or the `open` sees a failure indistinguishable from genuine un-instantiability \u2014 the open-sensitivity \u00a76e says no axiom line shows.", "created_at": "2026-07-28T16:32:17+08:00", "role": "horizon", "kind": "agent", "files": [{"path": "MainProjects/Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge/Algeb